## User Stories

### Kanad — Clubs Collection

Story CL-01: Create a Club Entry
As Aisha, I want to add a new club with its name, category, description, and weekly time commitment so students can find us on the platform.
Acceptance criteria: The admin form validates all fields. The club appears in the listing right after submission with no page reload needed.

Story CL-02: View All Clubs
As Alex, I want to see all the clubs listed on the platform so I can get a sense of what is out there.
Acceptance criteria: All clubs render as cards using vanilla JavaScript. Each card shows name, category, description, and weekly hours.

Story CL-03: Filter and Search Clubs
As Priya, I want to filter clubs by category or max weekly hours and search by name or keyword so I can quickly cut down the list to what actually works for my schedule.
Acceptance criteria: The search bar and dropdowns filter results dynamically without reloading the page.

Story CL-04: Edit a Club Entry
As Aisha, I want to update my club's information when things change so the listing stays accurate.
Acceptance criteria: The edit form pre-fills with current data. Changes save via PUT and reflect on the page immediately.

Story CL-05: Delete a Club Entry
As Aisha, I want to remove a club that is no longer active so the directory does not get cluttered with dead listings.
Acceptance criteria: A confirmation prompt appears before deletion. The card is removed from the list immediately after confirming.

Story CL-06: View Club Details and Members
As Alex, I want to click on a club and see its full details along with a list of students who have already joined, so I know what I am getting into.
Acceptance criteria: Clicking a club card opens a detail modal. The modal fetches and displays all members who have joined that club.

Story CL-07: Join a Club
As Alex, I want to register for a club by entering my personal details so I can become a member of that club.
Acceptance criteria: The join form accepts name, email, major, and year. If the user is logged in, the form auto-fills from their profile. On submit the user is saved to the users collection with that club in their joined clubs. If the email already exists, the club is added to their existing profile instead of creating a duplicate.

### Kanad — Membership Logs Collection

Story ML-01: Log a Club Experience
As Priya, I want to write up my experience in a club including how many hours it took, what I got out of it, and what was tough, so other students have something real to go off of.
Acceptance criteria: The form takes club name, member name, weekly hours, benefits, and challenges. The log shows up in the list right after submitting.

Story ML-02: View Club Experience Tab
As Alex, I want to scroll through membership logs grouped by club so I can see all the reviews for a specific club in one place.
Acceptance criteria: Logs are grouped by club name with a review count. Each card shows hours, benefits, and challenges.

Story ML-03: View Member Experience Tab
As any visitor, I want to see individual reviews with the member's name so I know who wrote each review and can trust it is from a real student.
Acceptance criteria: The Member Experience tab only shows logs that have a name attached. Anonymous logs are filtered out.

Story ML-04: Filter Logs and See Average Hours
As Alex, I want to filter logs for a specific club and see the average hours members actually spent, so I know what I am signing up for.
Acceptance criteria: Filtering by club name updates the list dynamically. The average weekly hours for that club appears above the results.

Story ML-05: Edit a Membership Log
As Priya, I want to go back and update my log if things changed over the semester so it stays accurate.
Acceptance criteria: Admin edit form pre-fills existing data. Changes save via PUT and update immediately.

Story ML-06: Delete a Membership Log
As Priya, I want to delete a log I wrote if it is no longer relevant.
Acceptance criteria: Confirmation before deletion. Card disappears from the list immediately.

### Aarya — Users Collection and Authentication

Story UP-01: Register an Account
As Alex, I want to create an account with my email and password so I can have a personal profile that persists across sessions.
Acceptance criteria: The registration form validates all required fields. Password is hashed before being stored. The user is logged in immediately after registering and redirected to the home page.

Story UP-02: Log In
As Priya, I want to log in to my existing account so I can access my profile and get a personalized experience.
Acceptance criteria: Login form validates email and password. On success the user object is stored in localStorage and the navbar updates to show the user's name.

Story UP-03: Edit My Details from Anywhere
As Priya, I want to click my name in the navbar and edit my profile details from any page so I do not have to navigate to the members page every time.
Acceptance criteria: Clicking the user's name in the navbar opens a modal with pre-filled fields. Saving updates the database and refreshes the navbar.

Story UP-04: Log Out
As Alex, I want to log out of my account from anywhere on the site so my session is cleared.
Acceptance criteria: Clicking Log Out in the user menu clears localStorage and redirects to the home page.

Story UP-05: Create a Profile
As Alex, I want to set up a profile with my name, major, year, bio, and interests so I have a presence on ClubMatch and can connect with people.
Acceptance criteria: The registration form validates all required fields. The profile is saved and visible in the members list immediately.

Story UP-06: View All Profiles with Tabs
As any visitor, I want to browse student profiles filtered by whether they have joined clubs or not, so I can find people with similar involvement levels.
Acceptance criteria: Three tabs — All, Members, and Students — filter the list dynamically. Each card shows a Member or Student badge.

Story UP-07: View a Full Profile
As any visitor, I want to click on a member card and see their full profile including bio, interests, and clubs.
Acceptance criteria: Clicking a card opens a profile modal with all details. No page reload.

Story UP-08: Delete a Profile
As Alex, I want to delete my profile if I decide I do not want to be on the platform anymore.
Acceptance criteria: Confirmation before deletion. Profile is removed from the members page immediately.

