## Design Mockups

### Page 1 — Home Page

Purpose: The landing page. Gives a quick introduction to ClubMatch and lets users jump into clubs, logs, or profiles.

Layout description: The top navigation bar shows ClubMatch on the left and Home, Clubs, Membership Logs, Members, Admin, and a Log In button on the right. When logged in, the Log In button is replaced by the user's first name with a dropdown for editing details and logging out. Below the navbar is a hero section with the headline Discover Your Favorite Club, a short tagline, a search bar with an orange search button, and category filter pills for All, Academic, Cultural, Sports, Professional, Arts, and Service. Below the hero is a How to Use ClubMatch section with four step cards explaining how to create a profile, browse clubs, read experiences, and join a club. Below that is a Featured Clubs grid showing 12 clubs with a View All Clubs button in the top right corner.

### Page 2 — Clubs Page

Purpose: The main club directory. Browse, filter, search, and join clubs. Admins can add, edit, and delete.

Layout description: Navigation bar at the top. A Clubs heading with an Add Club button visible only in admin mode. A filter bar with a search input, a category dropdown, and a max hours dropdown. A grid of club cards each showing a colored category icon, category badge, club name, description, weekly hours, and a click hint. Clicking a card opens a detail modal with full club information, a list of current members, and a Join This Club button. Clicking Join This Club opens a registration form that auto-fills from the logged-in user's profile if they are signed in.

### Page 3 — Membership Logs Page

Purpose: Where students read and submit membership logs. Two tabs separate club reviews from individual member reviews.

Layout description: Navigation bar at the top. A Reviews heading with a Log My Experience button visible to all users. Two tabs — Club Experience and Member Experience. A filter bar below the tabs. In Club Experience view, logs are grouped by club name with a review count badge and each card shows hours, benefits, and challenges. In Member Experience view, cards show a member avatar, their name, which club they are reviewing, and a View Details button that opens a modal with the full review.

### Page 4 — Members Page

Purpose: Student profiles. Create your own profile, browse other members, and view full profiles.

Layout description: Navigation bar at the top. A Members heading with a Create My Profile button that auto-fills from the logged-in user's data if they are signed in. Three tabs — All, Members showing students who have joined clubs, and Students showing students who have not joined any club yet. A search bar to filter by name or interest. Member cards showing an avatar, name, major, year, a green Member badge or blue Student badge, bio, interest tags, and joined clubs. Clicking a card opens a full profile modal.

### Page 5 — Login Page

Purpose: Let existing users log in to their account.

Layout description: A centered card on a dark gradient background. The ClubMatch logo at the top. Email and password fields. A Log In button. A link to the register page for new users. A Continue as guest link for users who just want to browse without an account.

### Page 6 — Register Page

Purpose: Let new users create an account.

Layout description: Same centered card layout as the login page. Fields for full name, email, password, major, year, bio, and interests. A Create Account button. A link back to the login page. A Continue as guest link.